        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "688266dc-d1cf-5c0e-86ab-fd7c9a62c225",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Angelique Kerber, Amélie Mauresmo, Andrea Petkovic, Victoria Azarenka\n- Events: 2015 Family Circle Cup – Singles, 2004 Summer Olympics\n- Topics: WTA rankings, Grand Slam singles titles\n\nFacts:\n- Amélie Mauresmo was born on 5 July 1979 and is a French former professional tennis player.\n- Amélie Mauresmo became a former world No. 1 in women's tennis.\n- Amélie Mauresmo won a silver medal at the 2004 Summer Olympics.\n- Amélie Mauresmo won two Grand Slam singles titles at the Australian Open and Wimbledon.\n- Andrea Petkovic was the defending champion at the 2015 Family Circle Cup – Singles.\n- Angelique Kerber defeated Andrea Petkovic in the semifinals of the 2015 Family Circle Cup – Singles.\n- Victoria Azarenka was the previous first-time new women's world No. 1 before Angelique Kerber, in 2012.\n- Angelique Kerber reached the world No. 1 ranking on 12 September 2016.\n- Angelique Kerber became the twenty-second and oldest player to achieve the women's No. 1 ranking for the first time on 12 September 2016.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
